## Requirements
(Capture required behaviors and outcomes as numbered requirements, not proposed implementations or technical solutions.)
Each requirement MAY carry an optional **acceptance** line — a single indented `- *Acceptance:*` bullet holding 1–3 semicolon-separated "done when…" clauses, each a short, plain-English, product-level outcome (NOT task/implementation steps, NOT Gherkin). Omit the line entirely when the outcome is self-evident.
<!-- Acceptance criteria are per-REQ "done when…" outcomes that confirm THAT requirement is met;
     Success metrics (below) are project-wide signals of overall success. Don't conflate the two. -->
<!-- OPTIONAL sub-grouping: when a project benefits, REQ-n MAY be clustered under headings:
       - Functional        — what the product does
       - Non-functional    — quality, security, performance, portability
       - Data & Schema     — entities, contracts, persistence, migration shape
       - UI-UX             — surfaces, flows, accessibility
       - AI-Agent          — for agentic builds: role, allowed + forbidden tools,
                             output contract, and when-to-stop conditions
     These are OPTIONAL groupings of the same REQ-n list, NOT required headers. A flat,
     ungrouped REQ list stays fully valid. The AI-Agent group is the genuinely new slot —
     renmark builds AI plugins, and agent role/tool-boundaries/output-contract/stop-rules
     are first-class requirements there, not implementation detail. -->

